## PHASE 2 — App Store Submission
### Objective: App approved and live on Apple App Store and Google Play
### Timeline: April 26 – May 9, 2026 (approx. 2 weeks)
### Commander's Intent: Get real users in hands via TestFlight first, then go public

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This phase has the most **waiting time** — Apple's review process is 1–7 days and is completely outside our control. Plan for it.

---

#### Task 2.1 — Set Up Apple Developer Account
**Who:** YOU (30 minutes)
**Cost:** $99/year

1. Go to [developer.apple.com/programs/enroll](https://developer.apple.com/programs/enroll/)
2. Sign in with your Apple ID (or create one)
3. Enroll as an **Individual** (not Organization — simpler for solo apps)
4. Pay $99
5. Wait for approval (usually same day, sometimes 24–48 hours)

**Done when:** You have an active Apple Developer account.

---

#### Task 2.2 — Set Up Google Play Console
**Who:** YOU (20 minutes)
**Cost:** $25 one-time

1. Go to [play.google.com/console](https://play.google.com/console)
2. Sign in with a Google account
3. Pay $25 registration fee
4. Accept developer agreement

**Done when:** Play Console account is active.

---

#### Task 2.3 — Privacy Policy + Terms of Service
**Who:** AI drafts, you review
**Why:** Both stores **require** a Privacy Policy URL before they'll accept your app. This is non-negotiable.

The AI will draft both documents appropriate for a coin collecting app (no financial transactions, no minors data, etc.) and we'll host them at `numista.ai/privacy` and `numista.ai/terms`.

**Done when:** Both pages live at your domain.

---

#### Task 2.4 — App Store Listing Content
**Who:** AI drafts, you review and approve

Items needed for both stores:
- App name: "Numista.AI — Coin Collector"
- Short description (80 characters)
- Full description (4,000 characters)
- Keywords (for search ranking)
- App screenshots (6–10 per device size) — AI generates these from the app
- App preview video (optional but recommended)
- Age rating questionnaire (you answer questions, AI guides you)
- Category: "Hobbies & Interests" / "Lifestyle"

**Done when:** All store listing assets ready to upload.

---

#### Task 2.5 — TestFlight Beta (iOS)
**Who:** AI builds the release, you install and test
**Why:** Before public submission, TestFlight lets up to 10,000 real users test the app with no App Store review delay.

You can add yourself, friends, and any coin club members as beta testers immediately. This is your real-world QA.

**Duration:** 1 week of beta testing

**Done when:** No critical bugs found in beta.

---

#### Task 2.6 — Google Play Internal Testing Track
**Who:** AI builds the release, you install and test
**Why:** Same as TestFlight — test on real Android devices before public release.

**Done when:** App tested on at least one Android device.

---

#### Task 2.7 — Submit for App Store Review
**Who:** AI prepares submission package, you click Submit in App Store Connect

Apple's review: 1–7 business days. They will either:
- **Approve** → goes live immediately
- **Reject with notes** → AI fixes the issues and we resubmit (adds 2–3 days)

Common first-time rejection reasons (we'll pre-empt all of these):
- Missing Privacy Policy *(handled in 2.3)*
- Placeholder UI *(handled in Phase 1)*
- No account deletion option *(AI will add this)*

**Done when:** "Ready for Sale" status in App Store Connect.

---

#### Task 2.8 — Submit for Google Play Review
**Who:** AI prepares, you submit

Google's review: typically 24–72 hours. Faster and more lenient than Apple.

**Done when:** App status "Published" in Play Console.

---

### Phase 2 Exit Gate ✅
- [ ] Apple Developer account active
- [ ] Google Play Console account active
- [ ] Privacy Policy + Terms live at numista.ai
- [ ] App approved on Apple App Store
- [ ] App approved on Google Play Store
- [ ] Both apps publicly downloadable

