## PHASE 3 — Build the Next.js Desktop Web App
### Objective: Replace Python/Streamlit site with a professional commercial web app
### Timeline: May 5–25, 2026 (approx. 3 weeks, overlaps with Phase 2 waiting time)
### Commander's Intent: Use App Store waiting time productively — build the web hub

> [!NOTE]
> This phase runs **in parallel with Phase 2 waiting time**. While Apple reviews your app (up to 7 days), we build the web platform. No time wasted.

---

### What the Next.js App Will Have

The desktop web app is the **research and management hub**. Think of it as your collector's command center:

| Section | What It Does |
|---|---|
| **Home / Dashboard** | Your collection stats, recent additions, market highlights |
| **My Collection** | Full sortable/filterable table of every coin you own |
| **Program Library** | Browse all 31 series, download checklists as PDF |
| **Coin Detail Page** | Full reference page per coin — images, grades, history, AI analysis |
| **AI Deepdive Chat** | Ask Gemini questions about any coin in your collection |
| **Wishlist** | Your want list with value tracking |
| **Account / Settings** | Profile, subscription tier (future), preferences |
| **About / Our Team** | The Numista.AI story |

Every page is SEO-indexed — so when someone Googles "1893-S Morgan Dollar value" they can potentially find your platform.

