## PHASE 4 — Integration, Polish, and Public Launch
### Objective: Both platforms live, tested, and announced
### Timeline: May 26 – June 6, 2026 (approx. 1.5 weeks)

---

#### Task 4.1 — Cross-Platform Account Testing
**Who:** YOU test, AI fixes

Verify that actions on the mobile app appear on the web, and vice versa:
- Scan a checklist on your phone → does it appear on the website?
- Mark a coin as owned on the website → does it appear in the app?

**Done when:** Full sync confirmed working.

---

#### Task 4.2 — Google Search Console Setup
**Who:** YOU (15 minutes) + AI guides
**Why:** This is how you tell Google that numista.ai exists and should be indexed. Free. Essential.

1. Go to [search.google.com/search-console](https://search.google.com/search-console)
2. Add numista.ai as a property
3. Verify ownership (AI will handle the code side)
4. Submit sitemap

**Done when:** Google confirms site is being crawled.

---

#### Task 4.3 — Performance Check
**Who:** AI
**What:** Run Google Lighthouse on the web app, fix any red flags. Target 90+ score on Performance and Accessibility.
**Duration:** 1 day

---

#### Task 4.4 — SDK Migration (Python backend)
**Who:** AI
**Why:** The `vertexai` SDK in the backend is deprecated — shutdown is **June 24, 2026**. Must be done before that date.
**What:** Migrate `scan_service/main.py` from `vertexai` SDK to the new `google-genai` SDK. Redeploy.
**Duration:** Half a day

> [!CAUTION]
> Do NOT skip this. If missed, the scan service will stop working on June 24, 2026.

---

#### Task 4.5 — Announce
**Who:** YOU
**What:** Tell people about it. Coin clubs, Reddit (r/coincollecting, r/coins), numismatic forums, any social media.

The AI can draft announcement copy if you want.

